What is here (src/ is the source, webvdb.mjs is the esbuild bundle that vdb-to-nvdb.mjs imports; rebuild with
`node scripts/vdb/vendor/webvdb/build.mjs`):
- src/nanovdb/*.ts   packages/vdb-web-tools/src/nanovdb/ unchanged: buildFromVdb, buildFromDense, quantize (fp8), writeNvdb.
- src/cpu/*.ts       packages/nanovdb-wgsl/src/cpu/{read-value,stride-tables,stride-tables.generated}.ts unchanged (CPU readValue, used by the parity check).
- src/nvdb-file.ts   packages/nanovdb-wgsl/src/nvdb-file.ts unchanged (NanoVDBFile). Its fflate import is aliased to src/fflate-stub.ts
                     (ZIP codec is not needed: we write and read codec NONE).
- src/vdb/*.ts       the Blosc-capable .vdb parser, copied from packages/runtime/vendor/vdb-web-tools/src (itself WebVDB's src/vdb/
                     plus the P4-H changes listed in that directory's NOTICE: select, constant tiles, pre-222 leaves, inactive-value
                     defaults, Blosc lz4). Houdini writes Blosc-compressed .vdb, which upstream's parser rejects.
- src/entry.ts, src/fflate-stub.ts, build.mjs   ours.
Nothing else from WebVDB is used. These files are not type-checked or linted by the workspace (scripts/ is outside tsconfig).
